1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,920
Ever since I was little, I've been having this same dream.

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,000
In it, I see this girl.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,520
She's someone I've never met.

4
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:16,820
I'm in love with her.

5
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:20,220
The kind of deep love you can only feel after a lifetime.

6
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,220
And she loves me back just as much.

7
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:29,980
But in the end, something freaky happens.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,840
The sky takes her back somehow.

9
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,060
And I wake up from the dream.

10
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:41,780
Unnerved and restless.

11
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:48,260
Hello, everyone.

12
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:51,640
Well, I'm Eishiro Sugata, resident genius.

13
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,220
This here is my assistant, pretty.

14
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:55,700
Hmm.

15
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:58,260
Look here.

16
00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:01,300
There appears to be some type of anomalous hole orbiting the Earth.

17
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,620
Scientists around the world have been working together to try and solve the mystery of its origin.

18
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:11,460
They've even dropped monitoring devices into the anomaly, but haven't settled on any logical conclusion.

19
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:15,480
But you see, their hypotheses are flawed because they are grounded in reality.

20
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:22,740
As I'm sure you're aware, Columbus, who discovered the Americas, was able to stand an egg on its end by simply thinking outside of the box.

21
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:28,000
This story illustrates that no one believes in the unreal until they see it for themselves.

22
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,320
It's the nature of people.

23
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,940
It's similar to the world beneath a girl's skirt.

24
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,020
Something truly a mystery.

25
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:37,920
But I have the ability to see.

26
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:41,120
I can see the key words that connect everything.

27
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,600
A whole new world.

28
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,780
Now, the next issue is what makes up this whole new world.

29
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:51,020
Speaking metaphorically, you could say that under the girl's skirt...

30
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:57,380
Tomo, come on!

31
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:58,660
Would you get up already?

32
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,180
We're gonna be late for school.

33
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,160
Just five more minutes.

34
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:05,980
For crying out loud, get up!

35
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:17,520
You know, I hear that's a good sign.

36
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,840
When the flag's full of mass first thing in the morning.

37
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:20,720
Come on.

38
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:21,340
No!

39
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:38,440
At least drink some milk before we head out.

40
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,800
Yeah, thanks.

41
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,840
And your tie's all messed up.

42
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:45,540
It doesn't matter how old you get, you still act like a child.

43
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:48,420
All right, let's get going.

44
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:53,620
We live in Sorami City.

45
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:56,800
It's a small town with a population of about 7,000.

46
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,760
Completely surrounded by mountains.

47
00:02:59,300 --> 00:02:59,840
It's nice.

48
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,560
The town isn't known for anything in particular.

49
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:06,700
If it was, it'd be the smile of the old farmer's face.

50
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:10,600
Or maybe the humongous 400-year-old cherry blossom tree

51
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,440
that sits on that hill right outside of town.

52
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,460
Reinforcing this sense of isolation...

53
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,980
Everyone always complains about how there's nothing to do here.

54
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:17,840
But I like it.

55
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,540
It's my kind of place.

56
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:21,080
My motto is this.

57
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,600
Peace and quiet is the only way to live.

58
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:27,600
I like to watch TV, eat, take a nap during class.

59
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,760
The most perfect thing you can ask for

60
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:32,160
is just a thread of peace and quiet running through your life.

61
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,260
Wouldn't you agree?

62
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:35,640
Save me.

63
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:39,180
The sky has me in its grip.

64
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:44,220
The sky has me in its grip.

65
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,160
Tomo!

66
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,540
Wake up!

67
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:48,340
Tomoki!

68
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,280
Class is over if you hadn't noticed!

69
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:58,320
You had the dream again, didn't you?

70
00:03:58,980 --> 00:03:59,660
Oh, great.

71
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:00,680
Am I crying?

72
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:03,240
Look, Tomoki.

73
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:06,340
You've been having that dream ever since you were a little kid.

74
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,800
Think maybe you should see a doctor about it or something?

75
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:10,180
It's just some stupid dream.

76
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,100
It's not like it's ruining my life or anything.

77
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:12,840
Okay.

78
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,660
Wait, I have an idea.

79
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:16,980
What if we run it by Sugata, see what he thinks?

80
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:18,540
No freaking way.

81
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,540
I don't want to get wrapped up with some dude

82
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:22,100
who just looks like he attracts trouble.

83
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:23,120
Hey, everyone come quick.

84
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,640
Some moron's about to jump off the roof.

85
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:26,940
Jump off the roof?

86
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,380
The wind is good today,

87
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:32,320
although I'm not exactly happy with the direction it's blowing.

88
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:34,640
But it won't be a problem for takeoff.

89
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:35,620
Don't do it!

90
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:36,360
You're in sight!

91
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:37,060
You'll die!

92
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:38,980
Oh, hello there, Miss President.

93
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:39,560
Good morning.

94
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,360
Um, is someone going to jump off the roof?

95
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,260
Take a look.

96
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:44,300
What?

97
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:45,280
Sugata!

98
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:46,860
Shouldn't you be trying to stop him?

99
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:49,500
I could ask him to come down, but he won't listen.

100
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:51,300
I'll worry about it after he falls.

101
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,740
Could you be more irresponsible?

102
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,720
I mean, you're student council president.

103
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:55,840
You've got to do something.

104
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:57,540
If you're talking about insurance,

105
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:58,960
I already bought a whole lot of it.

106
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:01,660
Several million worth of life insurance, to be exact.

107
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:02,700
Wow, that's a lot.

108
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,500
Don't you stand there acting all impressed?

109
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,520
Come on, Prez.

110
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:07,340
Aren't you two like childhood friends or something?

111
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,620
Shouldn't you show the tiniest bit of consideration?

112
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:12,560
Are you suggesting I'm not worried about him in the slightest?

113
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,800
No, that's not...

114
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,680
Are you suggesting I believe it might not be such a bad thing

115
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,920
to watch my dear friend plummet to his death

116
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,860
with a big smile spread across my face

117
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:22,840
as a cherry blossoms bloom in the background?

118
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:24,100
I didn't say that.

119
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:25,980
And are you suggesting I'm even considering

120
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:28,220
the remote possibility that after I've made my claim

121
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:29,780
on the insurance, I'll travel the world

122
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,300
on the finest luxury cruise liner

123
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,100
while I mourn my friend's untimely passing?

124
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,240
Are you?

125
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,440
What do you think?

126
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,000
Are you sure you want that answer?

127
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:37,920
No.

128
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:44,520
He jumped.

129
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:45,300
Be careful!

130
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:54,380
Oh.

131
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:57,960
So, you want to head back?

132
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,080
Hang on, Tomo.

133
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,040
What about your dream?

134
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:02,020
I am so not talking to that guy.

135
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,180
What are you talking about?

136
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:04,900
Tomo's just being stupid.

137
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:06,780
He wants to ask Sugata some questions.

138
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:10,280
We heard he's in the know regarding out there kinds of things.

139
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:11,900
You'd be right about that.

140
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:13,900
He's creepy, perverted beyond belief,

141
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,120
weird beyond comprehension,

142
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:15,880
and without a doubt,

143
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,500
the freakiest for a guy I know of.

144
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,520
But he's dependable for what you need.

145
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:20,640
Dependably nuts?

146
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,280
Well, who the hell else are we going to ask?

147
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,060
I mean, you refuse to go see a professional.

148
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:26,420
I just want to live in peace and quiet.

149
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:26,940
Fine, then.

150
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,680
Have it your way, jackass.

151
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:37,720
I understand every word of your concerns.

152
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:41,600
Many intelligent people believe dreams to be electrical signals

153
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,740
your brain sends out when processing memories.

154
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:44,660
In other words,

155
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:46,140
your desires or your memories

156
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:47,840
become your dreams during your sleep.

157
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:48,880
Okay.

158
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:52,400
But that's nothing more than a hypothesis grounded in reality,

159
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:55,080
and you can't explain the unreal using real terms.

160
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:57,100
Look at this.

161
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,000
No, not that.

162
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,540
You know what that is?

163
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:04,660
The black spot?

164
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:05,040
No.

165
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:06,140
Of course you don't.

166
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:06,520
What now?

167
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:09,220
Because you've already concluded you don't know.

168
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,680
There are scientists who've spent years researching this

169
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,700
and have yet to figure out the slightest thing about it.

170
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:15,120
But I understand it.

171
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:18,100
I know exactly what the true nature is behind this hole.

172
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:21,200
And of course, I also know what your dream means.

173
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:24,180
Both of them are part of a whole new world.

174
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:26,600
Such fools in the scientific community.

175
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,380
Something with this much mass,

176
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,740
this much displacement,

177
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:32,100
it can't be anything but a whole new world

178
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,060
floating over there.

179
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,280
This recurring dream you've been having

180
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,260
is also connected to this whole new world.

181
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,320
Have faith in me,

182
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:42,540
and I will unlock the mystery of this dream of yours.

183
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,460
That's great.

184
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:45,340
At precisely midnight tonight,

185
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:46,780
this whole new world of which I speak

186
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:47,880
will fly over this town.

187
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:50,040
Do you mind if I come check it out?

188
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:51,580
Sounds just fine.

189
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:53,480
This is bad.

190
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,960
I can already hear it.

191
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,960
The sound of my beautiful peace and quiet

192
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:58,440
being torn apart at the seams.

193
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,260
The cherry blossom tree

194
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:00,520
next to the shrine at midnight.

195
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,260
We're going to see this together.

196
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,400
I'm sorry,

197
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,120
but my mother told me

198
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,920
I can't stay out past midnight tonight.

199
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:13,180
Apologies.

200
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:14,560
Mikuko needs me tonight.

201
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,760
It doesn't look like I'll be able to join you.

202
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:19,780
To everyone who said

203
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:21,020
they'd come up here with me tonight,

204
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:21,960
thanks a lot.

205
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:22,900
I'm looking around,

206
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:23,560
and guess what?

207
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:24,240
No one.

208
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:25,480
Sincerely, Tomaki.

209
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:29,920
To hell with this.

210
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:30,720
I'm out of here.

211
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:34,040
Oh, it's Sugata.

212
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,480
Hey, what's up, weirdo?

213
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,960
Get the hell out of there.

214
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,400
I just did another pass

215
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,520
over the most recent data,

216
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,820
and something odd is going on.

217
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:43,560
I'm heading over the...

218
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:43,820
What?

219
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:44,880
You're breaking up.

220
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:45,560
I can't hear.

221
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:47,280
The hole is moving.

222
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:47,880
What?

223
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:49,340
You're in danger.

224
00:08:49,340 --> 00:09:04,980
Oh, no.

225
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,140
It's a person.

226
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:07,820
No.

227
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:09,780
It's not a person.

228
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,380
A person doesn't have...

229
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:14,800
A person doesn't have wings.

230
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:21,380
Don't think about how weird this is.

231
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:23,340
The whole mess just stinks of trouble.

232
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:24,520
Run away!

233
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,220
What the hell is happening?

234
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,160
It should be fine.

235
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:37,260
I'm sure of it.

236
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,960
The chick fell out of the freaking sky

237
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,020
without a scratch on her.

238
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,960
I'm not getting involved.

239
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:43,700
No way.

240
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,400
Peace and quiet is the best.

241
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,340
That's my motto,

242
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:47,480
and I'm sticking to it.

243
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:48,580
That's it.

244
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,800
That's what I say.

245
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,400
Those are the words I live by.

246
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:54,340
Oh, damn it!

247
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:08,420
Oh, man.

248
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,660
All I want is to live in peace.

249
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:14,620
After this, I'm gonna go home, watch TV,

250
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:15,900
and pass the hell out.

251
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:16,340
Ah...

252
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:16,660
Ah!

253
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:16,820
Ah.

254
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,800
Begin imprinting process.

255
00:10:40,800 --> 00:11:06,420
It is a pleasure to meet you, I am a pet class Angeloid, my purpose is to fulfill your every

256
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:35,380
want and desire. You are my master. Hey Tomo, I'm on cleaning duty today so I'm gonna head off to school. Get your ass out of bed so you're not late. Good morning, master.

257
00:11:36,420 --> 00:12:00,420
Master, please make a command. Give me any order that will please you. Anything you desire. Angeloids were created for the sole purpose of bringing our master's pleasure. It is all we know.

258
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:27,680
So whatever I want. Yes. You're... My what? Well, how about a bunch of cash? You are requesting a... That was almost weird. I was about to get my freak on with an alien creature from space or wherever. What's wrong with my head? Yeah, duh. If I had that much money, I could buy anything I wanted in the whole world. Initiating transfer.

259
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:32,680
You're screwing with my head. What is that card thingy? Let me see it. Hand it over.

260
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:37,680
In your language, this card would be known as a teleportation device.

261
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:42,680
Teleportation? I hear your request and all I need to do is order the required materials from the synapse. What's the synapse?

262
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:49,680
I have no stored information regarding the synapse. Those databanks are clear. After all, I have only just awoken so I am void of much data.

263
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:56,680
I am a pet class, Angeloid. My type is Alpha, Icarus. I was manufactured by the synapse for you.

264
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:59,680
I have no stored information regarding the synapse.

265
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:04,680
I have no stored information regarding the synapse. Those databanks are clear.

266
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:21,680
After all, I have only just awoken so I am void of much data. I am a pet class, Angeloid. My type is Alpha, Icarus. I was manufactured by the synapse for you. For your sole pleasure.

